process-free.m's freer spawned on the machine's GPU: each 1.6 MB array is
freed after its answer, and the next comes from the cache of large blocks,
so the most the process held at once is one array, rounded to 2 MiB, with a
few small blocks, not four. Freeing the string literal, which is in the
image's merk_static section, leaves it alone.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-free.m -o %t2
RUN: %gpu-env timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu | FileCheck %S/process-free.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_CHECK_PROCESS_MEMORY=1 MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines
CHECK:10: right
CHECK-NEXT:200000: right
CHECK-NEXT:200000: right
CHECK-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated
CHECK-NEXT:Mercury runtime: a GPU process held at most {{209[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]}} bytes of blocks at once
